<title>SWEDEN: TABLE - Electrolux swings to loss in H1.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Electrolux swings to loss in H1.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish household appliance group Electrolux posted these figures for the first six months of 1997 on Wednesday.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit/Loss after fin items  LOSS     264 vs  1,814 PROFIT</p>
<p> Sales					57,273 vs 57,012</p>
<p> EPS/Loss per share (Skr)     LOSS    5.40 vs 14.10 PROFIT</p>
<p> Operating profit			    432 vs  2,402</p>
<p> Operating costs			  56,841 vs 54,610</p>
<p> Net financial items	    CHARGE   696 vs    588 CHARGE</p>
<p> Minoriites				     47 vs    146</p>
<p> Tax						87 vs    639</p>
<p> Net result			   LOSS   398 vs  1,029 PROFIT</p>
<p> Depreciation				2,175 vs  2,234</p>
<p>* First half 1997 figures include restructuring costs of 2.5 billion crowns and a capital gain of 604 million crowns from the sale of Husqvarna Sewing Machines.</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuters poll found Electrolux was expected to post a loss after financial items of 305 million crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
